questions.stem:
Distinguish between level term assurance, decreasing term assurance, and convertible term assurance. For each type, describe:
(a) the structure of the sum assured;
(b) the primary market application in Nigeria; and (c) the key advantage and limitation of the product.

NIIRA 2025, Section 91(3), mandates credit life insurance for all loans exceeding ₦10 million. Critically evaluate the significance of this provision for:
(a) the life insurance industry's market opportunity in the banking and fintech lending space;
(b) the protection of Nigerian borrowers' families;
(c) the challenges of implementation, including product design, pricing, and regulatory compliance. Identify the opportunities and risks this mandate creates for life insurers seeking to develop embedded insurance propositions.
